% GORM model -> schema table — Tier FX FX.8.23. Replaces
% internal/linker/gorm_tables.go's LinkGormModelTables (Tier GT).
%
% Base facts (from the gorm_tables hub provider,
% internal/factpipe/hub_gorm_tables.go — resolving a GORM call's target
% table needs a model's own TableName() method body, a local variable's
% declared type read off its enclosing function/method's source span, or a
% .Model()/.Table() chain scanned a few lines above the call — none of
% which is a value already sitting in one node_meta column, so this is real
% Go over the graph-so-far, ported near-verbatim from the retired pass. See
% that file's doc comment for the full account):
%
%   gorm_query_edge(From, To, Model, Table)      a read reaching its table
%   gorm_persist_edge(From, To, Model, Table)     a write reaching its table
%   gorm_model_unresolved(Svc, File, Line, Model) a model with no table match
%   gorm_table_unresolved(Svc, File, Line, Table) a table name with no schema
%   gorm_table_collision(Svc, File, Line, Table)  a table name matching >1 node
%
% All five relations the emit spec consumes are pure pass-through — the hub
% already resolved the winning table (or ledgered why it couldn't) before
% asserting one fact per outcome.

gorm_query_edge_rel(From, To, Model, Table) :- gorm_query_edge(From, To, Model, Table).
gorm_persist_edge_rel(From, To, Model, Table) :- gorm_persist_edge(From, To, Model, Table).
gorm_model_unresolved_rel(Svc, File, Line, Model) :- gorm_model_unresolved(Svc, File, Line, Model).
gorm_table_unresolved_rel(Svc, File, Line, Table) :- gorm_table_unresolved(Svc, File, Line, Table).
gorm_table_collision_rel(Svc, File, Line, Table) :- gorm_table_collision(Svc, File, Line, Table).
